\f0\b \cf2 The replication package contains two folders: code, data
\f1\b0 \
\
The folder 
\f0\b code
\f1\b0  contains the following R scripts for setup, results, and supplemental analyses: \
\

\f0\b 01_setup_packages.R
\f1\b0 : load required packages for running subsequent scripts (note: should run this before running anything else)\

\f0\b 02_setup_functions.R
\f1\b0 : create custom functions for model estimation and output 
\f0\b \
03_setup_classify.R
\f1\b0 : show steps to produce the classification variable described in Appendix C.3 (note: this script is for illustration only, not required for analyses)
\f0\b \
04_results_prejudice.R
\f1\b0 : analyze main prejudice outcome (feelings about Muslims); produce Tables 2, D.10, and D.11
\f0\b \
05_results_religiousnatlm.R
\f1\b0 : analyze religious nationalism outcomes (statement approval); produce Tables 3, C.5, D.8, D.9, and D.12
\f0\b \
06_results_behavioral.R
\f1\b0 : analyze decider game and chat game outcomes; produce Tables C.6, C.7, C.8, C.9, C.10; Figure C.6
\f0\b \
07_results_mechanisms.R
\f1\b0 : analyze mechanisms; produce Figure 1
\f0\b \
08_supp_experience.R
\f1\b0 : analyze outcomes related to study experience for Appendices A and B
\f0\b \
09_supp_participation.R
\f1\b0 : analyze various measures related to participation (selection, response rates, conversation volume, attrition) in the experiment (Appendices C.1, C.2, C.3, and D.3)
\f0\b \
10_supp_robustness.R
\f1\b0 : perform a set of robustness checks described in Appendix D (Appendices D.4, D.7, D.8, D.9)
\f0\b \
11_supp_balance.R
\f1\b0 : perform balance tests (Appendix D.2)
\f0\b \
12_supp_hte.R
\f1\b0 : analyze various HTEs for the main prejudice outcome (Appendix E) \
\
The folder 
\f0\b data
\f1\b0  contains the following files: \
\

\f0\b 1. Completes_Merged_Anonymized.RData
\f1\b0 : main dataset featuring the 1,070 individuals who completed the conversation period; survey and experimental data merged and anonymized 
\f0\b \
2. Recruits_Anonymized.RData
\f1\b0 : dataset featuring the 2,684 eligible (Hindu/Muslim; in India; above 18; passed attention check) individuals who started the recruitment survey and either signed up or dropped out after learning about the main study
\f0\b \
3. Starts_Anonymized.RData
\f1\b0 : dataset featuring the 730 conversation threads that were started along with the characteristics of each thread (including whether it was completed) and its two participants; two observations per thread representing each participant in the thread
\f0\b \
4. codebook.xlsx
\f1\b0 : description of all variables included in Completes_Merged_Anonymized.RData, Recruits_Anonymized.RData, and Starts_Anonymized.RData\
\

\f0\b Steps for replication: 
\f1\b0 \
1. Set the working directory to the root folder\
2. Run 01_setup_packages.R\
3. Run whichever of scripts 04 to 12; all work independently, loading data and additional functions within\
\
The analyses have been carried out using R version 4.5.1 on macOS Sequoia 15.6.1}